# What a repository does not need.
#
# Everything NOT listed here is part of the game and its validation harness - and
# on GitHub Pages, everything not listed here is what gets published. So the list
# is short on purpose: nothing the browser loads is ever in it.
#
# See DEPLOY-ONLINE.md for the hosting story and README.md for the layout.

# dependencies (fbx2gltf, used by tools/fbx-*.js; the game itself has none)
node_modules/

# the generated deploy folder (tools/web-build.js makes it on demand), and the
# zip of the Deno relay, which is a build product of relay-deno.js
web/
deno-relay.zip

# probe logs and one-shot run output
*.log
*.err
*.out
*.pid

# the previous index kept while the prefix patch landed - not part of the game
index.html.bak-prefix

# source art the bake tools read. The game ships the *baked* results, so these
# are development material, not assets: chest_model.js, the .glb.js sidecars and
# the skin .glb files are what index.html actually asks for.
*.fbx
animated_old_chest.glb
cod-ghost-src/
Treasure_chest_(tier_1)-*.png
call-of-duty-ghost.zip

# editors, operating systems, and host scratch directories
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.vercel/
.netlify/
